WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.133
- [Narrator] If a disease breaks out

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.970
anywhere in the world,

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.030
the Epidemic Intelligence Service

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:11.040
or EIS is called in to
investigate the outbreak.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.220
- A lot of people refer to EIS

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.120
as the disease detectives

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.923
because we are the ones sent out

00:00:16.923 --> 00:00:20.773
during outbreak or emergency
response situations.

00:00:20.773 --> 00:00:23.570
- [Narrator] The elite team works quickly

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:24.858
to figure out who is sick,

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.574
the origin of the infection

00:00:26.574 --> 00:00:29.037
and how to stop it from spreading.

00:00:29.037 --> 00:00:32.037
(slow bright music)

00:00:34.977 --> 00:00:36.870
- I'm Caitlin Cossaboom.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.455
I'm a second year Epidemic
Intelligence Service Officer

00:00:39.455 --> 00:00:42.883
at the U.S. Centers for
Disease Control and Prevention.

00:00:43.825 --> 00:00:47.074
My first outbreak was an anthrax outbreak

00:00:47.074 --> 00:00:48.811
in wildlife in Namibia.

00:00:48.811 --> 00:00:52.992
Over 200 hippos and Cape buffalo died.

00:00:52.992 --> 00:00:56.970
Over a thousand people were
exposed to the carcasses.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.833
We assisted Namibia with control efforts

00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:02.962
in order to prevent future infections.

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:06.630
(slow bright music)

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:08.850
- [Narrator] Today, Caitlin
has been deployed here

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.220
on Saint Croix,

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:11.570
in the U.S. Virgin Islands.

00:01:13.085 --> 00:01:14.543
In September of 2017,

00:01:14.543 --> 00:01:17.970
the islands were hit by
two major hurricanes.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:20.360
In the aftermath several people fell sick

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.345
to a bacterial disease
called Leptospirosis.

00:01:23.345 --> 00:01:25.536
The first time it was seen on the islands.

00:01:25.536 --> 00:01:28.113
The local health department needed backup,

00:01:28.113 --> 00:01:31.355
so they called in the disease detectives.

00:01:31.355 --> 00:01:35.712
- Leptospirosis or Lepto is
a bacterial disease spread

00:01:35.712 --> 00:01:38.620
through the urine of infected animals.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.873
If there's flooding or rain,

00:01:40.873 --> 00:01:43.255
humans could have contact with water

00:01:43.255 --> 00:01:45.208
that has been contaminated.

00:01:45.208 --> 00:01:49.165
The symptoms of Lepto
are flu-like illness.

00:01:49.165 --> 00:01:52.646
But people that get a
very serious infection,

00:01:52.646 --> 00:01:54.723
it can be fatal.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:02.290
We have 14 people from CDC

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:04.000
that are down here

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.000
for this as well as at
least 25 local volunteers.

00:02:12.515 --> 00:02:13.810
We're gonna go back

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:16.339
to the block that we were in yesterday,

00:02:16.339 --> 00:02:18.523
um, yeah, so, it'll be pretty quick.

00:02:18.523 --> 00:02:21.320
- [Narrator] Once the team
has their map assignments

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.685
the detective work begins.

00:02:23.685 --> 00:02:27.695
We start going door to door

00:02:27.695 --> 00:02:30.770
with the primary goal of educating people

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:32.410
on the disease.

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.323
Hi, good afternoon.

00:02:34.323 --> 00:02:35.156
- Hi.

00:02:35.156 --> 00:02:36.280
- Hi, nice to meet you.
- I'm Mike.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:38.340
- We asked them if
they'd be willing to take

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:39.520
a survey.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:42.313
We take a small amount of
blood, so that we can test

00:02:42.313 --> 00:02:46.333
and see if they've been exposed to Lepto.

00:02:48.022 --> 00:02:50.750
The lab takes a specimen.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:54.120
The centrifuge will
spin down the specimens,

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.820
and then they'll store those for freezing

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.330
to be eventually mailed

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:01.144
back to CDC in Atlanta for the testing.

00:03:01.144 --> 00:03:04.000
What we're really hoping is

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:04.833
that the Department

00:03:04.833 --> 00:03:07.390
of Health can use that information

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:09.809
when paired with the survey data

00:03:09.809 --> 00:03:12.855
to identify risk factors for exposures.

00:03:12.855 --> 00:03:17.855
(slow bright music)

00:03:18.924 --> 00:03:21.741
I have a training in animal diseases

00:03:21.741 --> 00:03:25.040
and being able to apply that

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:29.258
to help humans is kind of
the best of both worlds.

00:03:29.258 --> 00:03:32.770
You're doing something

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.550
that is actively preventing people

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:39.216
from getting sick with
really serious diseases.

00:03:39.216 --> 00:03:41.053
Being out there

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:43.910
and doing that and interacting with people

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.610
and making that difference,

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:48.864
it's been a great experience.

00:03:48.864 --> 00:03:51.864
(slow bright music)

